{"explanation": "The unit responds most to dogs and dog-like animals shown large and close up. Activity is clearly higher when the animal fills a quarter or more of the frame, and highest when it fills most of it. It is weak for small or distant subjects. This size preference is the strongest and most reliable signal (rows 7 and 8, d +1.4 to +1.9), although similar units share it. There are weaker hints that it prefers subjects that are sharp, centered, cropped by the frame, and set against organic backgrounds without straight lines. The apparent preference for right-facing or camera-facing animals over left-facing ones did not replicate on new photos (row 1 fell to d +0.02). The no-straight-lines preference fell below the cutoff (percentile 92). So the direction and line effects are not reliable features of this unit.", "rows": [7, 8]}
```

